From 4773ea8cb3de340b3c7050058134d8f5e239ad9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:21:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a held review_model override moves to a free
 independent reviewer; review reroutes record the hold

Card t_4fffd0c7f2865cd2. Claude-implemented reviews waited on gpt-6-astra/openai-codex, pacing-held until
2026-11-20T22:40:20Z.

What #3362 (ed899d12ff) already covered: `resolve_dispatch_tier`, which admission, the pacing governor and pickup
all use, runs `paced_route` on the review route, and `_probe` moves `review_unpinned` off a far hold
(`held_pools`, `reroute_after_s`). The hub at 945ea5ad0d resolves all three named review cards (t_01cfba4ae08b29ee,
t_f5ae6712b53e34e3, t_4cf6ea0228db1fb9) to claude-fable-5-2/anthropic, read-only. The 17:20Z hold on
t_01cfba4ae08b29ee predates ed899d12ff.

Gaps closed here:
1. An explicit handoff `review_model` (`review_override`, and the registry substitute `review_override_refused`) on
   a far-held provider now falls back the same way. It takes the first `independent_routes(implementer)` route
   whose provider is neither held nor walled, and it must also pass this host's routing registry, because an
   override's peer is not limited to registry deep routes. The implementer's model is never used, a paced-only
   pool is never rerouted, and with no free peer the route stays and the governor holds the card.
2. A review run's `model_tier` receipt gets `paced: {provider, until, from}`: the held provider, its stored reset
   (None when unknown) and the route it replaced. `run_route.tier_reason` already names
   `<reason>+paced:<provider>`. A fault reading the receipt drops only that detail.

The card's spec put the check in `resolve_model_tier`. It went in `kanban_paced_reroute._probe` instead, so that
every reroute shares one hold test and one threshold. `resolve_model_tier` stays the pre-pacing base, as it is
for default routes, and the behaviour at the dispatch boundary is the same.

Not fixed (registry policy, follow-up card): pool-worker registries have no Fable deep route.
`independent_routes('claude-opus-5-5')` on worker-2 returns only gpt-6-astra/openai-codex, so a Claude-implemented
review evaluated on a worker has no independent reviewer free of holds, and rule 4 (never the implementer) keeps it
waiting.

Proof:
- New tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_review_paced_reroute.py: 34 tests over both entry paths (review lane, and a
  ready card with sdlc-review), driven through a real dispatcher tick. Covered: (a) held -> next free reviewer;
  (b) paced/open/near-reset -> unchanged; (c) no free reviewer -> held, not spawned, never the implementer;
  (d) held override and refused-override substitute -> fallback with the receipt; and the registry, require_model
  and class-override keeps. On base, 8 of them fail (override fallback and receipt).
- Unchanged suites test_kanban_model_tier_paced_reroute, test_kanban_review_model, test_kanban_model_tier and
  test_kanban_pin_reroute pass with no edits (167 tests incl. the new file).
- Mutants: 11 applied, 10 killed. The survivor is equivalent: the `is_review` guard on computing the receipt
  only skips work, because the payload already adds `paced` under `if is_review`.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok.
